01700020008004100037035002500078040002600103100002100129245001200150336002700162337002800189338002800217700002600245773002500271852002300296952004100319SNA00000370FCN-UNT20261106000000.0951207n########xx#           000 0 spad   a(FCN-UNT)SNA00000370  aFCN-UNTbspacFCN-UNT1 aKane,bJoseph W.10aFísica  atextobtxt2rdacontent  ano mediadobn2rdamedia  avolumenbnc2rdacarrier  aSternheim,bMorton M.0 w(FCN-UNT)SNA00000369  aFCN-UNTbSNAcPRES  3ej. 28PRESbSNAcPRESg91p0000638001746nam a2200445   SNA00000371FCN-UNT20261106000000.0951207s1986####ar#a          000 0 spad   a(FCN-UNT)SNA00000371  aFCN-UNTbspacFCN-UNT  aspa  aar#  a568.1  aA23e1 aArcucci,bAndrea Beatriz10aEstudio sistemático y evolutivo de un nuevo Tecodonte (Archosaurio, Cerritosauridae) del Triásico medio de La Rioja, Argentina3 aMaestría en Ciencias Biológicas orientación Zoología  a1a. ed.  aTucumánbFacultad de Ciencias Naturales e Instituto Miguel Lilloc1986  a55 h.bil., 20 fig., 7 lám. (con fot. color)c27,5 cm  atextobtxt2rdacontent  ano mediadobn2rdamedia  avolumenbnc2rdacarrier0 a10 aTesis para obtener el título de: ^tMaestría en Ciencias Biológicas orientación Zoología0 aDirector: Dr. José Fernando Bonaparte0 aBibliografía: 54-550 aNº orden interno TMZ 1  aTesis -- Universidad Nacional de Tucumán, Facultad de Ciencias Naturales e Instituto Miguel Lillo -- Magister en Ciencias Biológicas orientación Zoología -- 1986.  aZOOLOGIA.9FCN-UNT  aPALEONTOLOGIA.9FCN-UNT  aVERTEBRADOS.9FCN-UNT  aTECODONTES.9FCN-UNT  aLA RIOJA.9FCN-UNT  aARGENTINA.9FCN-UNT  aMAGISTER.9FCN-UNT  aFCN-UNTbSNAcPREShA23e92 ej.  3ej. 18PRESbSNAcPRESg350oA23ep00004183yTEXTO  3ej. 18PRESbSNAcPRESoA23ep00005077yTEXTO04523nam a2200493   SNA00000372FCN-UNT20261106000000.0951212s1995####xx#a          000 0 engd   a(FCN-UNT)SNA00000372  aFCN-UNTbspacFCN-UNT  aeng  anl---  a551.4(826.5)  aA23f1 aArcuri,bClaudia Beatriz10aFlood hazard assessment and zonation of the Medinas river catchment (Tucumán, Argentina)3 aMaestría en Geología  a1a. ed.  aEnschede, The NetherlandsbITCc1995  a119 p.bil., fot. (alg. color.), 4 mapas (en bols.)c29 cm.  atextobtxt2rdacontent  ano mediadobn2rdamedia  avolumenbnc2rdacarrier0 a20 aTesis: Magister en Geología0 aDirector of Studies: Ir. R. Soeters, ITC, Enschede0 aBibliography at the end of each chapter0 aAnnex: p. 4103-1190 aNº de orden interno: TMG 2  aTesis -- International Institute for Aerospace Survey and Earth Sciences -- Master of Science in Applied Geomorphology -- 1995.  aThe Medinas river catchment is located in the province of Tucumán, northwestern Argentina. The catchment coordinates are: 27º 11' S.L. \ 66º 12' W.L. for the north-western corner, and 27º 28' S.L. \ 65º 24' W.L. for the south eastern one. The Medinas river is formed by the confluence of the Cochuna and Las Cañas rivers, at 600 m.a.s.l., on the Nevados del Aconquija Mountain Range footslope. Situated east of the Andes, the area is in the humid sub-tropical zone. In the study area, river flooding occurs repeatedly (almost every year), causing loss and damage to property, decreasing agricultural production rates, causing soil erosion, uncontrolled sedimentation, and bank erosion; what in a broad sense, causes deterioration in the standard of living of the local population. The cost of this flooding, in terms of direct and indirect economic, and socio-economic effects, in addition to the physical destruction that occurs, has not been assessed. Relevant amount of money, at present invested in relief supplies for flood-ravaged communities, compensation for affected farmers, and protection works, could be saved if flood mitigation measurements could be taken in advance. Investments to prevent flooding, account of provincial government for the 1993-95 period, reaches as high as US$ 67,637, for flood protection works of the Medinas river. The social and economic crisis occurring in the province of Tucumán, claims for urgent mitigation measurements to be taken about the flooding problem. In order to mitigate flooding effects, it is essential to have maps compiling the flood characteristic (extent, depth, duration, frequency, intensity), as well as, be aware of the causes and processes responsible for such flooding. Since these primary elements were not available, they were produced through this work. With the availability of these data, was possible to carry out the flood hazard assessment and zonation. The necessity of flood hazard assessment and zonation became clear after the devastating floods of 1986 and 1992 (the largest floods on record). In this work, a Geomorphic Approach to flood hazard assessment and zonation has been chosen. The approach integrates both: geomorphological data with indirect flood data; gathered from remote sensing imagery, fieldwork data, and reports. Due to the absence of detailed topographic and hydrological data. The flood hazard zonation map could be refined when more flood and hydrological data (recurrence interval, discharge data) area available. The study intends to set out a basis for future hazard mapping, and mitigation programmes in the region, since little (or even none) has previously been done. By using the flood hazard zonation map, damage assessment, and planning of emergency and relief operations could be done.  aGEOLOGIA.9FCN-UNT  aCIENCIAS DE LA TIERRA.9FCN-UNT  aGEOMORFOLOGIA.9FCN-UNT  aGEOMORFOLOGIA APLICADA.9FCN-UNT  aRIEGOS NATURALES.9FCN-UNT  aINUNDACION FLUVIAL.9FCN-UNT  aARGENTINA.9FCN-UNT  aTUCUMAN.9FCN-UNT  aRIO MEDINAS.9FCN-UNT  aMAGISTER.9FCN-UNT  aFCN-UNTbSNAcPREShA23f91 ej.  3ej. 18PRESbSNAcPRESg100oA23fp00006357yTESIS00460nab a2200169   450000100120000000300080001200500170002000800410003703500250007804000260010333600270012933700280015633800280018477300250021285