 aEjemplar fotocopiado0 aBibliografía al final0 anº de orden interno: S-56  aSEMINARIO -- Universidad Nacional de Tucumán, Facultad de Ciencias Naturales -- Licenciado -- 1979.  aThe present paper is the first of a series of revisions concerning Argentine and South American Hemerobiidae (Neuroptera-Planipennia). A general account of the family and a key for Argentine-Chilean genera are given. The generus Megalomus Rambur 1842 in Argentina and Chile is particularly treated, with the recognition of two subgenera: Megalomus and Pirionius. The genera Pirionius Navás 1926 and Spinomegalomus Nakahara 1965 are synonymized with Megalomus. The following new Synonymy is indicated: Megalomus linguatus Navás 1910 - Megalomus intricatus Navas 1914 = Megalomus infuscatus Navás 1914 = Megalomus princeps Navás 1932 = Megalomus nanus Navás 1933 = Megalomus bridaroll Navás 1933. A new species: Megalomus stangei is described. The paper is completed with schemes, photographs and maps.-  aZOOLOGIA.9FCN-UNT  aSEMINARIO.9FCN-UNT  aHEMEROBIIDAE.9FCN-UNT  aPLANIPENNIA.9FCN-UNT  aINSEPTOS.9FCN-UNT  aENTOMOLOGIA.9FCN-UNT  aFCN-UNTbSNAcPRESh595.791 ej.  3ej. 18PRESbSNAcPRESg10o595.7p00001401ySEMINARIO01490nam a2200445   SNA00003832FCN-UNT20261106000000.0010418s1956####mx#a          100 0 spad   a(FCN-UNT)SNA00003832  aFCN-UNTbspacFCN-UNT  aspa  amx#  a553. (061.3)  aS68s1 aGonzález Reyna,bJenaro2 nCongreso Geológico Internacionaln20d4 al 11 de Septiembre de 195610aSYMPOSIUM sobre yacimientos de manganeso  aMéxicob/Stylo/c1956  a5 t.bil., mapas y tablas (interc. en tomos) ; 23,5 cm.  atextobtxt2rdacontent  ano mediadobn2rdamedia  avolumenbnc2rdacarrier0 aContenido:0 at.1: el manganeso en general0 at.2: Africa0 at.3: América0 at.4: Asía y Oceanía0 at.5: Europa  aYACIMIENTOS.9FCN-UNT  aMANGANESO.9FCN-UNT  aMINERIA.9FCN-UNT  aEXPLOTACION MINERA.9FCN-UNT  aGEOLOGIA.9FCN-UNT  aFCN-U