T  aSternheim,bMorton M.0 w(FCN-UNT)SNA00006102  aFCN-UNTbSNAcPREShK131p2E93 ej  3ej. 38PRESbSNAcPRESg93,50oK131p2Ep00007856yTEXTO05673nam a2200433   SNA00007887FCN-UNT20261106000000.0070829s2006####ar#a          000 0 spad   a(FCN-UNT)SNA00007887  aFCN-UNTbspacFCN-UNT  aspa  aar#  a581.5(826.2)  aB739r1 aBravo,bSandra Josefina del Valle10aRegimen de fuego en una sabana del Chaco Occidental y sus efectos morfológicos en especies leñosas  aTucumánbUniversidad Nacional de Tucumán, Facultad de Ciencias Naturales e Instituto Miguel Lilloc2006  axi,117 h.bil.,fig.,fot.color,Gráf.mapa , 29,5 cm. (Incluye CDRom con texto completo)  atextobtxt2rdacontent  ano mediadobn2rdamedia  avolumenbnc2rdacarrier0 aDirector: Dr. Carlos Kunst0 aCo-Director: Dr. Ricardo Grau0 aBibliografía: h. 108-1170 aNº de orden interno: TDB 17  aTesis -- Universidad Nacional de Tucumán, Facultad de Ciencias Naturales e Instituto Miguel Lillo -- Doctora en Ciencias Biológicas Orientación Botánica -- 2006.  aAs a disturbance, fire is one of the most important ecological factors in the Argentinean Chaco Region. It affects remarkably the landscape and species that have both varied in time and with use intensity. Objectives of this thesis were: to analiyze effects of fire on a set of woody native species, to evaluate their potentiality for dendroecologic studies about fire regimen, to determine frequency and intensity of fires in a typical Chaco's savanna nad to study the relation between rais and fire occurrence. A sabanna of E. muticus was selected as study area due to the continuity of fine fuels (necessary for scars and expansion of fire) and presence of of woody species able to register fires. Fire effects on native woody species were analyzed at external and anatomical level. A fire chronology was determined by standard dendroecology methods. An indirect indicadtor of the fire intensity was select. Fire-rainfall relationships on interannual scale were analysed using superposed epoch analysis performed employing the program FHX2. The formation of scars and fire marks were determined in Aspidosperma quebracho-blanco, Schinopsis lorentzii, Prosopis alba, and Prosopis nigra. Fire scars were more severe wounds, with precentage of damage to bole perimeter average of 12,2 per cent (DS 17,1) and they produced an interruption of xilem growth. Fire marks were slight wounds, with percentage of damage to bole perimeter average of 4,6 per cent (DS 4,6) without interruption of txylem growth. Acacia aroma and Acacia furcatispina produced only fire scars. Fire scars induced modifications on shape of bole by forminf ribs and inclusive bark while fire marks formed separations of woody layers. Both wouns affected the stem at different poinst and sometimes, without continuity or specific orientation. The nark thickness was seemengly an important agent to prevent the fire damage and its was greater among tree species than shrubby species. Connected to this, the ability to close fire wounds was higher in early specoes. Wounds staterrrrrrrd discolloration of the xylem formed before the damaga. The xylem formed after the fire showed higger pernetage of parenchyma and a lesser percentage of vessels and fibres. Decolorate wood and changes on precentage of woody elements would increase pathogen attacks and alterate wood technological such us resistance and durability. The ability of A. quebracho-blanco, S. lorentzii, A. aroma and A. furcatispina to generate recognizable fire wounds and annual growth rings together with their longevity and phyto-sanitarian state made their use obtain the first fire chronology of a argentinean Chaco enviironment by dendroecological techniques. It was state that the height of wounds on stem is a reliable intensity index of past fires. A fire chronology from 1925 to 1996 was made for E. muticus savanna. The fire mean frequency estimated was 0.179 fires/ año-1 and the mean fire interval was 3.38 years. The height of wouns indicated that 70 per cent of the fires were of moderate to higs intensity. Results allow to establish a high-frecquency fire regime and moderate to high intensity. Within fire chronology an increment of the frequency fire frequency was determined from 1970. The highest fire frequency period coincide with more rainfalls in studed area. Years with fire event had bigger precipitations than years without fire. In addition, it was determined that more spread fires occured two years after one with rainfalls above the average. This seems to uncover the existence of climatic control on the fuel production to burns. Results of this thesis suggest that under the actual fire regime wouls remain savannah structure due to the sensitivity of shrubby species to fire. However, it may be altered by climate and land use intensivity. The information of the last century fire regimen characterisstics will allow adjusting protocols of prescribed burns and this way to ensure continuity of resources within savannas of Chaco region.  aBOTANICA.9FCN-UNT  aECOLOGIA VEGETAL.9FCN-UNT  aFUEGO.9FCN-UNT  aPERTURBACION (ECOLOGIA).9FCN-UNT  aREGION CHAQUEÑA.9FCN-UNT  aCHACO.9FCN-UNT  aSANTIAGO DEL ESTERO.9FCN-UNT  aARGENTINA.9FCN-UNT  aTESIS.9FCN-UNT  aFCN-UNTbSNAcPREShB739r91 ej.  3eej. 18PRESbSNAcPRESg300oB739rp00007941yTESIS01728nam a2200469   SNA00007888FCN-UNT20261106000000.0070830s2006####ar#           000 0 spad   a(FCN-UNT)SNA00007888  aFCN-UNTbspacFCN-UNT  aspa  aar#  a556.55(826.5)  ab969E1 aBustos,bMaría Soledad10aEvaluación de la calidad del agua, en el río Lules, (Tucumán-Argentina)  aTucumánbUniversidad Nacional de Tucumán, Facultad de Ciencias Naturales e Instituto Miguel Lilloc2006  a71 h.îil.,fig.,fot.,gráf.,tablas , 29,5 cm.  atextobtxt2rdacontent  ano mediadobn2rdamedia  avolumenbnc2rdacarrier0 aDirectora: Dra. Beatriz Tracanna de Albornoz0 aCo-Director